---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Methodology | Crypto Yield Archive" description="How Crypto Yield Archive classifies, verifies, and presents crypto lending and yield platform history.">
  <section class="panel hero-panel">
    <p class="eyebrow">Definitions & limits</p>
    <h1>Methodology</h1>
    <p>Crypto Yield Archive is a historical registry, not a live APY ranking, investment recommendation, or real-time dashboard.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid two-col" style="margin-top:18px;">
    <div class="detail-stack">
      <section class="panel card">
        <h2>Core principles</h2>
        <p>CYA records platform history, customer outcome, terms risk, failure chain, and evidence. Unknown values are preserved instead of forcing guesses.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel card">
        <h2>Scope</h2>
        <p>The current registry focuses on CeFi lending platforms, crypto interest accounts, centralized yield platforms, and borrowing/lending services.</p>
        <p>Exchange Earn, DeFi lending protocols, yield aggregators, pool-level records, deployment-level records, real-time APY, and real-time TVL are not prioritized in the initial registry scope.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel card">
        <h2>Counting unit</h2>
        <p>CYA counts platform entities. Products, pools, vaults, chain deployments, and individual claim classes are not separate platform records unless they become historically meaningful records of their own.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel card">
        <h2>Record model</h2>
        <div class="fact-grid">
          <div class="fact"><div class="k">platform_entity</div><div class="v">The platform or historically meaningful yield service.</div></div>
          <div class="fact"><div class="k">platform_event</div><div class="v">Timeline events such as withdrawal pauses, bankruptcy filings, restructuring, and distributions.</div></div>
          <div class="fact"><div class="k">platform_evidence</div><div class="v">Sources backing entity, event, outcome, terms-risk, or URL-history claims.</div></div>
          <div class="fact"><div class="k">customer_outcome</div><div class="v">What happened to user funds, including partial repayment, ongoing claims, no recovery, or unknown outcomes.</div></div>
          <div class="fact"><div class="k">terms_risk</div><div class="v">How platform terms, product category, or legal process affected asset-treatment uncertainty.</div></div>
          <div class="fact"><div class="k">product_profile</div><div class="v">Interest accounts, lending products, Earn-like products, and other historically relevant yield offerings.</div></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel card">
        <h2>Evidence and reliability</h2>
        <p>Preferred sources include official statements, court documents, bankruptcy documents, regulatory notices, archived pages, and reputable reporting.</p>
        <p>Reliability is marked as high, medium, or low. Lower-reliability records are surfaced on the Source quality page and should not be treated as definitive.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel card">
        <h2>URL handling</h2>
        <p>Original URLs are preserved as historical records. For ended or repurposed platforms, archived URLs should be preferred and unsafe domains should not be treated as normal outbound links.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel card">
        <h2>Corrections</h2>
        <p>A good correction should include the platform name, CYA page URL, the field or claim that appears wrong, source links, and a short explanation.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="panel card sticky-side">
      <h2>Related views</h2>
      <div class="side-links">
        <a class="archive-link" href="/source-quality/">Source quality</a>
        <a class="archive-link" href="/terms-risk/">Terms risk</a>
        <a class="archive-link" href="/outcomes/">Customer outcomes</a>
        <a class="archive-link" href="/failures/">Failure reasons</a>
        <a class="archive-link" href="/stats/">Registry stats</a>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
